{{!-- A single repo calls it for its only app (appName). Call it at the top level of a document: hasRootScript reads the context it is called from. --}}
{{#if (isMono)}}
An app that listens on a port takes it from the `PORT` environment variable. To change the port of one app, run its script from its directory:

{{#each apps}}
{{#if (appUrl appName)}}
- {{appName}}: `{{#inDirectory "apps" appName}}PORT=4000 {{runScript "dev"}}{{/inDirectory}}`
{{/if}}
{{/each}}

`PORT` on the root `{{runScript "dev"}}` reaches every app, which then all listen on that port.{{#if (hasRootScript "start")}} `start` takes it the same way.{{/if}}
{{else}}
The app listens on port {{appPort appName}}. Set `PORT` to listen on another one: `PORT=4000 {{runScript "dev"}}`.{{#if (hasRootScript "start")}} `start` takes it the same way.{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "tooling" "portless")}}

`dev` and `start:portless` run through portless, which assigns the port itself and ignores `PORT`: set `PORTLESS_APP_PORT` to pin it.
{{/if}}
